<title>CANADA: Canada labor income data release postponed to June.</title>
<headline>Canada labor income data release postponed to June.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The May 2 release of labor income estimates for February has been postponed to June 2, Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said the reason was the recent rescheduling of payroll data for February. The agency admitted last month to making a significant error in its calculation methods and would therefore delay the payroll data to May 6.</p>
<p>A federal election is scheduled for June 2.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
